From 2a6720162f349137f565d5c90b87ad5e41b62055 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: spotUP <retroranksmail@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 00:02:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] upkg browse: launch an installed add-on from its Launch line

Enter on an installed row whose control file carries a Launch: line leaves curses, runs the line through xsystem (sh -c, so the program's stack cookie is honoured by ixemul execve), resumes browse and reloads the rows. The exit code shows in the status line as NAME exited with code N. Remove moves from r to Delete. Footer hints come from ch_menu_hints.
---
